  <node id="DOC_Dfed6d84a0e4f">
    <data key="label">Dfed6d84a0e4f: Is the metaverse failing</data>
    <data key="type">document</data>
    <data key="detail">[PDF excerpt omitted in delivery snapshot]</data>
  </node>
  <edge id="e1" source="T01" target="TH_PRIVACY">
    <data key="relation">topic-associated-with-threat</data>
    <data key="weight">1.0</data>
    <data key="evidence">Accept: Perceived personal-information privacy risks associated with adoption of metaverse business/finance services. Limits: Perception/adoption evidence does not establish actual privacy breaches. The human-identity-threat construct on p.8 concerns AI/workplace existential issues, not identity theft.</data>
    <data key="edge_origin">author_reviewed_k11_20261001</data>
    <data key="qualifiers">perception_evidence; p8_human_identity_construct_is_not_identity_theft</data>
  </edge>
  <edge id="e2" source="T02" target="TH_CYBER">
    <data key="relation">topic-associated-with-threat</data>
    <data key="weight">1.0</data>
    <data key="evidence">Modify: Modify: retain as “smart-contract vulnerability and project-anomaly detection”. Limits: A proposed/evaluated technical method; does not establish prevention in live use or cover all cyberattack types.</data>
    <data key="edge_origin">author_reviewed_k11_20261001</data>
    <data key="qualifiers" />
  </edge>
  <edge id="e3" source="T02" target="TH_IDENTITY">
    <data key="relation">topic-associated-with-threat</data>
    <data key="weight">1.0</data>
    <data key="evidence">Promote: Avatar-cloning/impersonation risks addressed by a proposed detection/privacy-awareness framework. Limits: Described scenarios and a test-bed do not establish real-world victimisation or preventive effectiveness.</data>
    <data key="edge_origin">author_reviewed_k11_20261001</data>
    <data key="qualifiers" />
  </edge>
  <edge id="e4" source="T02" target="TH_PAYMENT">
    <data key="relation">topic-associated-with-threat</data>
    <data key="weight">1.0</data>
    <data key="evidence">Modify: Modify: retain as “ML-based detection/classification of suspected fraudulent or malicious Ethereum/Bitcoin transactions”. Correct the seven-algorithm-ensemble description. Limits: Classification results and stated aims do not demonstrate a reduction in actual fraud or operational deployment.</data>
    <data key="edge_origin">author_reviewed_k11_20261001</data>
    <data key="qualifiers">ml_classifier_comparison_not_seven_algorithm_ensemble</data>
  </edge>
  <edge id="e5" source="T02" target="TH_PRIVACY">
    <data key="relation">topic-associated-with-threat</data>
    <data key="weight">1.0</data>
    <data key="evidence">Promote: Personal-information and behavioural-data privacy exposure addressed by the proposed NFT-avatar framework; replace the generic “data” keyword rationale. Limits: Do not claim measured breaches or field-proven prevention.</data>
    <data key="edge_origin">author_reviewed_k11_20261001</data>
    <data key="qualifiers" />
  </edge>
  <edge id="e6" source="T04" target="TH_CYBER">
    <data key="relation">topic-associated-with-threat</data>
    <data key="weight">1.0</data>
    <data key="evidence">Promote: Attacks on avatar/virtual-entity trust and reputation systems, including Sybil, on/off and reputation manipulation. Limits: Included under the agreed scope covering associated platform-security risks. A direct financial-offence mechanism is not established.</data>
    <data key="edge_origin">author_reviewed_k11_20261001</data>
    <data key="qualifiers">trust_reputation_system_attacks_only; no_payment_specific_or_financial_offence_mechanism</data>
  </edge>
  <edge id="e7" source="T05" target="TH_GOVERNANCE">
    <data key="relation">topic-associated-with-threat</data>
    <data key="weight">1.0</data>
    <data key="evidence">Modify: Modify: retain as “audit/compliance governance and jurisdictional accountability challenges”; add the jurisdiction chapter when discussing actual gaps. Limits: Recommendations do not establish control effectiveness. The chapter supplies the authors' legal analysis, not an independent verification of current law.</data>
    <data key="edge_origin">author_reviewed_k11_20261001</data>
    <data key="qualifiers" />
  </edge>
  <edge id="e8" source="T05" target="TH_PRIVACY">
    <data key="relation">topic-associated-with-threat</data>
    <data key="weight">1.0</data>
    <data key="evidence">Promote: Observed data-collection/disclosure inconsistencies and associated privacy exposure in the applications studied by METAseen. Limits: Do not generalise to all metaverse applications or imply proven legal violations or crime incidence.</data>
    <data key="edge_origin">author_reviewed_k11_20261001</data>
    <data key="qualifiers">metaseen_applications_only_no_legal_violation_claim</data>
  </edge>
  <edge id="e9" source="T05" target="TH_SCAM">
    <data key="relation">topic-associated-with-threat</data>
    <data key="weight">1.0</data>
    <data key="evidence">Accept: Accept on Author C’s supplied passage: retain as a general fraud concern motivating audit controls. The independent source-check limitation remains recorded. Limits: A general fraud concern; no specific scam mechanism, incident rate or laundering pathway is established.</data>
    <data key="edge_origin">author_reviewed_k11_20261001</data>
    <data key="qualifiers">general_fraud_concern_only; source_check_limitation_recorded</data>
  </edge>
  <edge id="e10" source="T06" target="TH_SCAM">
    <data key="relation">topic-associated-with-threat</data>
    <data key="weight">1.0</data>
    <data key="evidence">Accept: Accept with the stated perception caveat: “interviewed artists' perceived scam and suspicious-activity risks in NFT markets”. Limits: Interviews do not independently establish that alleged crimes occurred or measure their incidence. Keep the perception qualification visible.</data>
    <data key="edge_origin">author_reviewed_k11_20261001</data>
    <data key="qualifiers">perception_evidence; interviews_do_not_establish_crimes_or_incidence</data>
  </edge>
  <edge id="e11" source="T07" target="TH_IDENTITY">
    <data key="relation">topic-associated-with-threat</data>
    <data key="weight">1.0</data>
    <data key="evidence">Accept: Accept: “identity/impersonation risks motivating avatar authentication”. Limits: A motivating risk, not an incident-frequency estimate. Supports the authentication strand more directly than the transaction-protocol strand.</data>
    <data key="edge_origin">author_reviewed_k11_20261001</data>
    <data key="qualifiers" />
  </edge>
  <edge id="e12" source="T08" target="TH_DEFI">
    <data key="relation">topic-associated-with-threat</data>
    <data key="weight">1.0</data>
    <data key="evidence">Accept: Accept: describe literature-discussed DeFi-related laundering/concealment mechanisms. Limits: Keep the p.11 finding that NFTs did not prompt an en masse switch away from established methods. That NFT-specific finding does not establish that all DeFi laundering is rare. No adoption-frequency estimate follows from the edge.</data>
    <data key="edge_origin">author_reviewed_k11_20261001</data>
    <data key="qualifiers">manning_nft_specific_finding_no_en_masse_switch_p11; no_adoption_frequency_estimate</data>
  </edge>
  <edge id="e13" source="T08" target="TH_GOVERNANCE">
    <data key="relation">topic-associated-with-threat</data>
    <data key="weight">1.0</data>
    <data key="evidence">Accept: Accept with a narrow regulatory explanation: “supervisory and cross-jurisdiction governance challenges concerning DeFi/DEX activity”. Limits: A descriptive analysis of regulation and supervisory challenges; does not demonstrate effectiveness of particular measures.</data>
    <data key="edge_origin">author_reviewed_k11_20261001</data>
    <data key="qualifiers" />
  </edge>
  <edge id="e14" source="T08" target="TH_SCAM">
    <data key="relation">topic-associated-with-threat</data>
    <data key="weight">1.0</data>
    <data key="evidence">Accept: Accept: retain as literature discussion of cryptoasset fraud/scams. The Manning anchor supplies independently checked support even while Shim's PDF is unlocated. Limits: Review/case-synthesis material; not new measurement by this project. Maintain attribution to the cited literature.</data>
    <data key="edge_origin">author_reviewed_k11_20261001</data>
    <data key="qualifiers">review_case_synthesis_not_new_measurement</data>
  </edge>
  <edge id="e15" source="T08" target="TH_WALLET">
    <data key="relation">topic-associated-with-threat</data>
    <data key="weight">1.0</data>
    <data key="evidence">Promote: Cross-chain/asset-hopping laundering exposure using bridges and decentralised exchanges; replace the Shim wallet-credential-theft rationale with Manning p.8, §9.1. Limits: Source support overlaps the DeFi edge and is not an additional independent incident finding. Credential theft alone does not establish laundering.</data>
    <data key="edge_origin">author_reviewed_k11_20261001</data>
    <data key="qualifiers">support_overlaps_T08_DEFI_edge_not_independent; credential_theft_alone_not_laundering</data>
  </edge>
  <edge id="e16" source="T09" target="TH_NFT">
    <data key="relation">topic-associated-with-threat</data>
    <data key="weight">1.0</data>
    <data key="evidence">Accept: Accept: “NFT-market manipulation risks discussed in the source”. Limits: Monetary and incident claims are attributed to other references. The relationship can be accepted without repeating the unverified monetary figure.</data>
    <data key="edge_origin">author_reviewed_k11_20261001</data>
    <data key="qualifiers" />
  </edge>
  <edge id="e17" source="T10" target="TH_CYBER">
    <data key="relation">topic-associated-with-threat</data>
    <data key="weight">1.0</data>
    <data key="evidence">Promote: Potential quantum attacks on encryption/access-control security and the proposed post-quantum response. Limits: Retain the potential/future-risk framing; do not imply observed operational quantum attacks, measured crime incidence or field-proven protection.</data>
    <data key="edge_origin">author_reviewed_k11_20261001</data>
    <data key="qualifiers">potential_future_quantum_risk_only; no_observed_operational_quantum_attacks</data>
  </edge>
  <edge id="e18" source="T10" target="TH_PRIVACY">
    <data key="relation">topic-associated-with-threat</data>
    <data key="weight">1.0</data>
    <data key="evidence">Accept: Accept: “privacy/data-protection concerns motivating encryption and access control”. Limits: A technical research motivation and proposed scheme; not measurement of actual breaches or proof of operational prevention.</data>
    <data key="edge_origin">author_reviewed_k11_20261001</data>
    <data key="qualifiers" />
  </edge>
  <edge id="e19" source="T11" target="TH_CYBER">
    <data key="relation">topic-associated-with-threat</data>
    <data key="weight">1.0</data>
    <data key="evidence">Accept: Accept: general platform-security threat discussion. Limits: A threat-landscape overview, not an incident-prevalence study.</data>
    <data key="edge_origin">author_reviewed_k11_20261001</data>
    <data key="qualifiers" />
  </edge>
  <edge id="e20" source="T11" target="TH_DEFI">
    <data key="relation">topic-associated-with-threat</data>
    <data key="weight">1.0</data>
    <data key="evidence">Modify: Modify: retain specifically as “exploitation of smart-contract vulnerabilities”. Limits: Do not extend the entry to all DeFi/DAO/governance misuse. It is a threat-table entry, not a detailed case study.</data>
    <data key="edge_origin">author_reviewed_k11_20261001</data>
    <data key="qualifiers">smart_contract_vulnerability_exploitation_only</data>
  </edge>
  <edge id="e21" source="T11" target="TH_GOVERNANCE">
    <data key="relation">topic-associated-with-threat</data>
    <data key="weight">1.0</data>
    <data key="evidence">Accept: Accept: general legal/compliance and cross-border governance challenges. Limits: Does not establish a particular accountability-gap incident or evaluate a governance intervention.</data>
